Article 3 (Types of Uniforms and Designs)
(1) Uniforms worn by juvenile reformatory personnel, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "uniforms") shall be classified into work uniforms and accessories. <Amended on December 27, 2007>
(2) Uniforms shall be classified as follows, and their designs shall be separately determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Justice: <Amended on March 27, 2019; February 7, 2022>
1. Work uniforms shall be classified as follows:
  (a) Formal uniforms;
  (b) Field-duty uniforms;
  (c) Sanitary uniforms;
  (d) Winter overcoats;
  (e) Rainwear.
2. Accessories shall be classified as follows:
  (a) Work shoes;
  (b) Insignia (chest and sleeve insignia);
  (c) Name tags.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), the design of uniforms worn by juvenile reformatory personnel, etc. working at a Juvenile Delinquency Prevention Center may be separately determined by the head of each Center, taking into account the nature of the duties and budgetary limits. <Newly inserted on March 27, 2019; February 7, 2022>
